Adjacent to this, browsers also reset `ended` synchronously when a seek is initiated, so:

```js
video.play();
await new Promise(resolve => audio.addEventListener("ended", resolve, { once: true }));
video.currentTime = 0;
console.log(video.ended)
```

will print `false`. The spec says that `ended` only reflects the state at step 1 of the event loop, so it should technically print `true`. A clause should probably be added to the `ended` attribute to say that it is false if a seek was initiated after step 1, and a seek step added to refer to that.

If there is more interest in the PR mentioned above, I can amend it with this improvement as well.
